    "summary": "A man&#039;s shirt, which falls just below the knee.  Made of undyed cream-coloured tabby woven cotton cloth; commercially produced.  A straight panel, both front and back, with three additional panels, and two small diamond-shaped gussets, create an A-line shape; machine-stitched.  &#039;V&#039; neck opening and a small, pointed collar with self-colour embroidery, using cotton threads.  The sleeves, which are sewn at right angles to the body of the shirt, are gathered onto a wide cuff, which also has self-colour embroidery.  A line of pulled thread work at the hem of the shirt.  Some discolouring.",
